/*Write a Java program that prompts the user for a float value and converts the given number of type float into integer data type.

Input Format:
  - The input is the floating point value.

Output Format:
  - The output is the integer after the data type conversion.

Note: A partial code is provided in the editor.*/
//////////////////////////////////////
/* Logic: Casting truncates toward zero (7.9 gives 7, -7.9 gives -7).*/

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        float f = sc.nextFloat();
        int result = (int) f;          // explicit narrowing cast truncates the decimal part
        System.out.println(result);
        sc.close();
    }
}
